YOUR TASK: Complete this task: Implement the primary solver using the left/top edge gauge: for each test case, scan rows left-to-right maintaining row_prefix (parity of A to the left) and col_prefix[j] (parity of A above); for each B cell union row i with column W+j in a weighted XOR DSU with weight 1 ^ row_prefix ^ col_prefix[j]; check that every row and column has even A parity; if any parity is odd or the DSU is inconsistent output 0, otherwise output pow(2, components, 998244353). Use fast buffered I/O and a path-compressing weighted DSU, and report the sample test verdict.